{"id":"mahabharata-13-057","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":57,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 57 · Yudhishthira's sorrow at the empty earth","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira says that he is confused as he thinks again and again how the earth has been stripped of kings, and sees the wives who were left without husbands and the houses emptied. Vaishampayana tells of Bhishma's reply on the gift of cows and of the worlds that await the one who gives a gift to a brahmin, and the Pandavas and Draupadi approve his words.","kn":"ಭೂಮಿ ರಾಜರಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಬರಿದಾದುದು, ಪತಿಯಿಲ್ಲದ ಪತ್ನಿಯರು, ಖಾಲಿ ಮನೆಗಳನ್ನು ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ಚಿಂತಿಸಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಗೊಂದಲಗೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಗೋದಾನ, ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರಿಗೆ ದಾನ ಮಾಡುವವನಿಗೆ ಕಾದಿರುವ ಲೋಕಗಳ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಉತ್ತರವನ್ನು ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು, ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಅನುಮೋದಿಸಿದರು.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि राजाओं से रिक्त पृथ्वी और पतिहीन स्त्रियों तथा सूने घरों को बार-बार सोचकर वे व्याकुल हैं। वैशम्पायन गोदान और ब्राह्मण को दान देने वाले के लिए प्रतीक्षारत लोकों पर भीष्म का उत्तर बताते हैं, और पाण्डव तथा द्रौपदी उनकी बात का अनुमोदन करते हैं।","te":"రాజులు లేక ఖాళీ అయిన భూమి, భర్తలు లేని స్త్రీలు, ఖాళీ ఇళ్లను మళ్లీ మళ్లీ ఆలోచించి తాను కలత చెందుతున్నానని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అంటాడు. గోదానం, బ్రాహ్మణునికి దానం ఇచ్చేవాని కోసం వేచి ఉన్న లోకాలపై భీష్ముని జవాబును వైశంపాయనుడు చెబుతాడు; పాండవులు, ద్రౌపది ఆమోదిస్తారు.","ta":"மன்னர்களற்ற வெறுமையான பூமி, கணவரற்ற மனைவியர், காலியான வீடுகளை மீண்டும் மீண்டும் எண்ணித் தாம் குழம்புவதாக யுதிஷ்டிரர் கூறுகிறார். பசுதானம், அந்தணருக்குக் கொடுப்பவனுக்குக் காத்திருக்கும் உலகங்கள் பற்றிய பீஷ்மரின் பதிலை வைசம்பாயனர் கூற, பாண்டவர்களும் திரௌபதியும் ஏற்கின்றனர்.","ml":"രാജാക്കന്മാരില്ലാതെ ഭൂമി ശൂന്യമാകുന്നത് ആവർത്തിച്ച് ചിന്തിക്കുമ്പോൾ, ഭർത്താക്കന്മാരില്ലാതെ ഉപേക്ഷിക്കപ്പെട്ട ഭാര്യമാരെയും ശൂന്യമായ വീടുകളെയും കാണുന്നുവെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറഞ്ഞ് സംശയത്തിലാകുന്നു. പശുദാനത്തെക്കുറിച്ചും ബ്രാഹ്മണന് ദാനം നൽകുന്നവരെ കാത്തിരിക്കുന്ന ലോകങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചും ഭീഷ്മരുടെ മറുപടി വൈശമ്പായനൻ പറയുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരും ദ്രൗപദിയും ആ വാക്കുകളെ അംഗീകരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.57; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मुह्यामीव निशम्याद्य चिन्तयानः पुनः पुनः ।\nहीनां पार्थिवसंघातैः श्रीमद्भिः पृथिवीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am bewildered, thinking again and again today of this earth bereft of its hosts of glorious kings."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्राप्य राज्यानि शतशो महीं जित्वापि भारत ।\nकोटिशः पुरुषान्हत्वा परितप्ये पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having obtained hundreds of kingdoms and conquered the earth, Bharata, and having killed men by the million, I am tormented, grandfather."}},{"n":3,"text":"का नु तासां वरस्त्रीणामवस्थाद्य भविष्यति ।\nया हीनाः पतिभिः पुत्रैर्मातुलैर्भ्रातृभिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"What will now become of the state of those fine women who are bereft of husbands, sons, maternal uncles and brothers?"}},{"n":4,"text":"वयं हि तान्गुरून्हत्वा ज्ञातींश्च सुहृदोऽपि च ।\nअवाक्शीर्षाः पतिष्यामो नरके नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed those elders, kinsmen and friends, we shall surely fall headfirst into hell; of this there is no doubt."}},{"n":5,"text":"शरीरं योक्तुमिच्छामि तपसोग्रेण भारत ।\nउपदिष्टमिहेच्छामि तत्त्वतोऽहं विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I wish to mortify my body with fierce austerity, Bharata; lord of the people, I want to be instructed truly about it here.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य तद्वाक्यं श्रुत्वा भीष्मो महामनाः ।\nपरीक्ष्य निपुणं बुद्ध्या युधिष्ठिरमभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Yudhishthira's words, great-minded Bhishma examined him closely with his mind, and spoke to him."}},{"n":7,"text":"रहस्यमद्भुतं चैव शृणु वक्ष्यामि यत्त्वयि ।\nया गतिः प्राप्यते येन प्रेत्यभावेषु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Listen, I will tell you a wonderful secret: by what means one reaches a destination in the states after death, Bharata."}},{"n":8,"text":"तपसा प्राप्यते स्वर्गस्तपसा प्राप्यते यशः ।\nआयुःप्रकर्षो भोगाश्च लभ्यन्ते तपसा विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"By austerity heaven is gained, by austerity fame; long life and enjoyments too are obtained by austerity, mighty one."}},{"n":9,"text":"ज्ञानं विज्ञानमारोग्यं रूपं संपत्तथैव च ।\nसौभाग्यं चैव तपसा प्राप्यते भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowledge, realization, health, beauty, prosperity and good fortune are obtained through austerity, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":10,"text":"धनं प्राप्नोति तपसा मौनं ज्ञानं प्रयच्छति ।\nउपभोगांस्तु दानेन ब्रह्मचर्येण जीवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One gains wealth by austerity; silence gives knowledge; enjoyments come through giving, and life through celibacy."}},{"n":11,"text":"अहिंसायाः फलं रूपं दीक्षाया जन्म वै कुले ।\nफलमूलाशिनां राज्यं स्वर्गः पर्णाशिनां भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fruit of non-violence is beauty; of initiation, birth in a good family; those who eat fruits and roots gain a kingdom, and those who eat leaves, heaven."}},{"n":12,"text":"पयोभक्षो दिवं याति स्नानेन द्रविणाधिकः ।\nगुरुशुश्रूषया विद्या नित्यश्राद्धेन संततिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who lives on milk goes to heaven; by bathing one becomes rich; by serving a teacher one gets learning; by daily ancestral rites, offspring."}},{"n":13,"text":"गवाढ्यः शाकदीक्षाभिः स्वर्गमाहुस्तृणाशनात् ।\nस्त्रियस्त्रिषवणस्नानाद्वायुं पीत्वा क्रतुं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One rich in cattle comes from vows of eating greens; they say grass-eating leads to heaven; women who bathe thrice daily, and who live on air, gain a sacrifice."}},{"n":14,"text":"नित्यस्नायी भवेद्दक्षः संध्ये तु द्वे जपन्द्विजः ।\nमरुं साधयतो राज्यं नाकपृष्ठमनाशके ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who bathes daily becomes skilled; a twice-born who mutters prayers at both twilights gains a kingdom; one who endures the desert, and fasts to death, reaches the vault of heaven."}},{"n":15,"text":"स्थण्डिले शयमानानां गृहाणि शयनानि च ।\nचीरवल्कलवासोभिर्वासांस्याभरणानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who sleep on bare ground, there are houses and beds; for those wearing bark and rags, clothes and ornaments;"}},{"n":16,"text":"शय्यासनानि यानानि योगयुक्ते तपोधने ।\nअग्निप्रवेशे नियतं ब्रह्मलोको विधीयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"for an ascetic engaged in yoga, beds, seats and vehicles; and for one who enters fire by rule, the world of Brahma is ordained."}},{"n":17,"text":"रसानां प्रतिसंहारात्सौभाग्यमिह विन्दति ।\nआमिषप्रतिसंहारात्प्रजास्यायुष्मती भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By abstaining from flavours one finds good fortune here; by abstaining from meat one has long-lived offspring."}},{"n":18,"text":"उदवासं वसेद्यस्तु स नराधिपतिर्भवेत् ।\nसत्यवादी नरश्रेष्ठ दैवतैः सह मोदते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who lives in water becomes a ruler of men; the truthful, best of men, rejoice with the gods."}},{"n":19,"text":"कीर्तिर्भवति दानेन तथारोग्यमहिंसया ।\nद्विजशुश्रूषया राज्यं द्विजत्वं वापि पुष्कलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fame comes from giving, health from non-violence, and from serving brahmins a kingdom or abundant twice-born status."}},{"n":20,"text":"पानीयस्य प्रदानेन कीर्तिर्भवति शाश्वती ।\nअन्नपानप्रदानेन तृप्यते कामभोगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving water one gains lasting fame; by giving food and drink one is satisfied in all desires and enjoyments."}},{"n":21,"text":"सान्त्वदः सर्वभूतानां सर्वशोकैर्विमुच्यते ।\nदेवशुश्रूषया राज्यं दिव्यं रूपं नियच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who comforts all beings is freed from all sorrows; by serving the gods one gains a kingdom and divine beauty."}},{"n":22,"text":"दीपालोकप्रदानेन चक्षुष्मान्भवते नरः ।\nप्रेक्षणीयप्रदानेन स्मृतिं मेधां च विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving lamps and light a man becomes sharp-sighted; by giving things worth seeing he gains memory and intelligence."}},{"n":23,"text":"गन्धमाल्यनिवृत्त्या तु कीर्तिर्भवति पुष्कला ।\nकेशश्मश्रून्धारयतामग्र्या भवति संततिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By abstaining from perfumes and garlands one gains abundant fame; for those who wear their hair and beard long, the finest offspring."}},{"n":24,"text":"उपवासं च दीक्षां च अभिषेकं च पार्थिव ।\nकृत्वा द्वादश वर्षाणि वीरस्थानाद्विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fasting, initiation and bathing, king, performed for twelve years, are better than the hero's station."}},{"n":25,"text":"दासीदासमलंकारान्क्षेत्राणि च गृहाणि च ।\nब्रह्मदेयां सुतां दत्त्वा प्राप्नोति मनुजर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving a daughter in a brahmin marriage, best of men, one gains servants, ornaments, fields and houses."}},{"n":26,"text":"क्रतुभिश्चोपवासैश्च त्रिदिवं याति भारत ।\nलभते च चिरं स्थानं बलिपुष्पप्रदो नरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through sacrifices and fasts one goes to heaven, Bharata; and one who offers offerings and flowers gains a long-lasting place."}},{"n":27,"text":"सुवर्णशृङ्गैस्तु विभूषितानां\nगवां सहस्रस्य नरः प्रदाता ।\nप्राप्नोति पुण्यं दिवि देवलोक-\nमित्येवमाहुर्मुनिदेवसंघाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives a thousand cows adorned with golden horns gains merit and a heavenly world; so say the hosts of sages and gods."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रयच्छते यः कपिलां सचैलां\nकांस्योपदोहां कनकाग्रशृङ्गीम् ।\nतैस्तैर्गुणैः कामदुघास्य भूत्वा\nनरं प्रदातारमुपैति सा गौः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a tawny cow with a cloth, a bronze milk-pail, and gold-tipped horns: that cow becomes a wish-fulfilling cow, with all those qualities, and comes to the giver."}},{"n":29,"text":"यावन्ति लोमानि भवन्ति धेन्वा-\nस्तावत्फलं प्राप्नुते गोप्रदाता ।\nपुत्रांश्च पौत्रांश्च कुलं च सर्व-\nमासप्तमं तारयते परत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"The giver of a cow gains as many fruits as the cow has hairs; and he saves his sons, grandsons and his whole family to the seventh generation in the next world."}},{"n":30,"text":"सदक्षिणां काञ्चनचारुशृङ्गीं\nकांस्योपदोहां द्रविणोत्तरीयाम् ।\nधेनुं तिलानां ददतो द्विजाय\nलोका वसूनां सुलभा भवन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who gives a brahmin a cow of sesame with a fee, with lovely golden horns, a bronze pail, and a cloth upon her, the worlds of the Vasus are easily attained."}},{"n":31,"text":"स्वकर्मभिर्मानवं संनिबद्धं\nतीव्रान्धकारे नरके पतन्तम् ।\nमहार्णवे नौरिव वायुयुक्ता\nदानं गवां तारयते परत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a wind-driven boat on a great ocean, the gift of cows carries across in the next world a man bound by his own deeds who is falling into the hell of fierce darkness."}},{"n":32,"text":"यो ब्रह्मदेयां तु ददाति कन्यां\nभूमिप्रदानं च करोति विप्रे ।\nददाति चान्नं विधिवच्च यश्च\nस लोकमाप्नोति पुरंदरस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a maiden in brahmin marriage, makes a gift of land to a brahmin, and gives food by rule, gains the world of Indra."}},{"n":33,"text":"नैवेशिकं सर्वगुणोपपन्नं\nददाति वै यस्तु नरो द्विजाय ।\nस्वाध्यायचारित्रगुणान्विताय\nतस्यापि लोकाः कुरुषूत्तरेषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives a brahmin who is rich in study and good conduct a perfectly furnished dwelling will also gain the worlds among the Northern Kurus."}},{"n":34,"text":"धुर्यप्रदानेन गवां तथाश्वै-\nर्लोकानवाप्नोति नरो वसूनाम् ।\nस्वर्गाय चाहुर्हि हिरण्यदानं\nततो विशिष्टं कनकप्रदानम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving draught animals, cows and horses, a man gains the worlds of the Vasus. They say gold given leads to heaven, and a gift of fine gold is better still."}},{"n":35,"text":"छत्रप्रदानेन गृहं वरिष्ठं\nयानं तथोपानहसंप्रदाने ।\nवस्त्रप्रदानेन फलं सुरूपं\nगन्धप्रदाने सुरभिर्नरः स्यात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving an umbrella one gets an excellent house; by giving sandals, a vehicle; by giving clothes, a handsome form; by giving perfumes, a man becomes sweet-smelling."}},{"n":36,"text":"पुष्पोपगं वाथ फलोपगं वा\nयः पादपं स्पर्शयते द्विजाय ।\nस स्त्रीसमृद्धं बहुरत्नपूर्णं\nलभत्ययत्नोपगतं गृहं वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who gives a brahmin a tree bearing flowers or fruits gains, without effort, a house rich in women and full of many jewels."}},{"n":37,"text":"भक्षान्नपानीयरसप्रदाता\nसर्वानवाप्नोति रसान्प्रकामम् ।\nप्रतिश्रयाच्छादनसंप्रदाता\nप्राप्नोति तानेव न संशयोऽत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"A giver of food, drink and flavours obtains all flavours in abundance; the giver of shelter and covering obtains just those, without doubt."}},{"n":38,"text":"स्रग्धूपगन्धान्यनुलेपनानि\nस्नानानि माल्यानि च मानवो यः ।\nदद्याद्द्विजेभ्यः स भवेदरोग-\nस्तथाभिरूपश्च नरेन्द्रलोके ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives brahmins garlands, incense, perfumes, ointments, baths and wreaths will be free of disease and handsome, in the world of kings."}},{"n":39,"text":"बीजैरशून्यं शयनैरुपेतं\nदद्याद्गृहं यः पुरुषो द्विजाय ।\nपुण्याभिरामं बहुरत्नपूर्णं\nलभत्यधिष्ठानवरं स राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives a brahmin a house, furnished with beds and not lacking in seed, delightful and full of many jewels, gains an excellent place, king."}},{"n":40,"text":"सुगन्धचित्रास्तरणोपपन्नं\nदद्यान्नरो यः शयनं द्विजाय ।\nरूपान्वितां पक्षवतीं मनोज्ञां\nभार्यामयत्नोपगतां लभेत्सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who gives a brahmin a bed with fragrant, varied coverings gains, without effort, a beautiful, charming wife who comes with her family."}},{"n":41,"text":"पितामहस्यानुचरो वीरशायी भवेन्नरः ।\nनाधिकं विद्यते तस्मादित्याहुः परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who lies on the hero's bed becomes a follower of Brahma; the great sages say there is nothing higher than that.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":42,"text":"तस्य तद्वचनं श्रुत्वा प्रीतात्मा कुरुनन्दनः ।\nनाश्रमेऽरोचयद्वासं वीरमार्गाभिकाङ्क्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, the delighted descendant of Kuru did not choose to dwell in a hermitage, longing for the hero's path."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरः प्राह पाण्डवान्भरतर्षभ ।\nपितामहस्य यद्वाक्यं तद्वो रोचत्विति प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira said to the Pandavas, best of Bharatas, \"Let the grandfather's words please you.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"ततस्तु पाण्डवाः सर्वे द्रौपदी च यशस्विनी ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य तद्वाक्यं बाढमित्यभ्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Pandavas and the glorious Draupadi honoured those words of Yudhishthira, saying \"Certainly.\""}}]}]}